{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1139376-help-blood-vintners","id":1139376,"title":"Help: Blood Vintners","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-11T01:15:24-07:00","id":1139376,"title":"Help: Blood Vintners","content":"So in 1.0 there was a writeup somewhere about blood vintners. It went into the attitudes and methods of vintner practitioners and was really quite a thoroughly detailed bit of writing to help you get into the mindset of a snobbish blood-trading vampire.<br /> <br /> And I cannot find it for the life of me. I'm pretty certain it wasn't in the Marcellarius bloodline writeup, and I've gone through the Ventrue clanbook several times but no luck. Any ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T08:47:25-07:00","id":1139455,"title":"","content":"Might it have been in the Ghouls suplement? It was where Lacrima and Blood Wine were introduced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T09:06:55-07:00","id":1139462,"title":"","content":"The only thing I can think of offhand is the Invictus covenant book made a brief reference to kindred who go around tasting blood from as many different rare and exotic animals and people and often hold events in the same vein as a wine tasting party. But they didn't get any specific weird powers or abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T12:19:12-07:00","id":1139514,"title":"","content":"Yeah I found both of those, neither is it, although the Invictus one was close.<br /> <br /> It wasn't about powers or abilities. The one I'm thinking of went through descriptions of collecting specifically rare individuals for their flavour, and that the vintner will often wax lyrical about the blood's flavour but the whole thing being less about the taste than it is about the culture of exclusivity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T03:06:09-07:00","id":1139668,"title":"","content":"Are you sure it was for Requiem? It sounds suspiciously similar to an excerpt from a Masquerade book that was posted in one of the Blogs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T13:28:28-07:00","id":1139756,"title":"","content":"Sounds a lot like the Society of Gourmands that I use for My City of Arkham....<br /> <br /> Not sure where I got it from, but it has been a staple for years.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>The Society of Gourmands</b></i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Society of Gourmands, formed by Danica Lane in Arkham, is a group of kindred connoisseurs who have drawn together out of an appreciation for the delight of Vitae, not as a form of sustenance but as the only true pleasure left to them in their new existence. Members of the Society are akin to wine-tasters, they enjoy wine not for the sake of its pleasant alcoholic effects, but for it's taste. Every three months a member will throw a banquet for the benefit of all the other members, free of charge, with the most delicious and new flavors of vitae he can find.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Soiree is members only, no freeloaders allowed. The event itself is elaborately planned, though each Host chooses how much to spend on their event. Indeed, some have hosted Soiree's in empty warehouses to great effect as the barren environs draws attention to the vitae, but there is a tendency for friendly (and sometimes not so friendly) competition to out do each other. The main course often consists of several Kine that are sampled by the attendee\u2019s, they\u2019re left mercifully unconscious because serving dead food is not only considered pass\u00e9 but literally bad taste, and killing the Kine at a Soiree is the epitome of it. Though the Society is neither highly moral nor highly amoral, it does tend towards the latter. Members are encouraged not to kill Kine unnecessarily, but are otherwise left to their own devices. The Society does not enforce or espouse any tenets, but it does expect its members to follow a simple code of conduct.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> There is more if you are interested...<br /> Let me know... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T18:53:08-07:00","id":1139808,"title":"","content":"Thorbes, got a link? I swear it was a Requiem reference but I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> Tymeaus, thanks for the offer but currently I'm just trying to collate canon material on the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":1487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","user":"Zahaqiel","date":". 09-12-2017, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T04:45:18-07:00","id":1139876,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/5-essential-tips-to-becoming-a-successful-vitaephile-vampire-the-masquerade/\" target=\"_blank\">Might be this, might be not...</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 09-13-2017, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T19:09:41-07:00","id":1140064,"title":"","content":"Try searching the various books for Mandragora. There might be a blurb in the Circle book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.th